-- title:
--   Finitely many zeros and poles of ̄ j on the special fibre
-- statement:
--   Fix $N \geq 1$ and a prime $p$ with $p \nmid N$, and let $c : X \to \operatorname{Spec} \mathbb{Z}_{(p)}$ be a proper, smooth of relative dimension $1$ morphism from an integral scheme, where $\mathbb{Z}_{(p)}$ denotes the subring [`GaloisRep.ratLocalizedAt p`](def/GaloisRep_Flat.html#L8) of rationals whose denominator is coprime to $p$. The data are: a `CurveModel` $M_0$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ of the modular function field `modularFunctionFieldFull N` (the subfield of $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ generated by the $q$-expansions $j(q^d)$, $d \mid N$) together with an isomorphism $e_0$ onto the rational fibre of $c$ over the base; a section $\varepsilon_{\inf}$ of $c$; a closed point $x_0$ of $M_0.C$ whose place is the $q$-adic cusp `cuspInftyFull N`, and a $\mathbb{Q}$-point $y$ of the rational fibre factoring through $\varepsilon_{\inf}$ and mapping to $x_0$ under $e_0^{-1}$; a `CurveModel` $M_\eta$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ of `modularFunctionFieldBar N` with an isomorphism $e_\eta$ onto the geometric generic fibre, equivariance of `pointEquivPlace` for the arithmetic Galois action (`hgal`), and compatibility (`hcompat`) asserting that the valuation subring of the place of a geometric point pulls back, along `baseChangeEquiv` composed with `Algebra.TensorProduct.includeRight`, to the valuation subring of the place of the corresponding closed point of $M_0$; for every valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $p \in A$ non-unit, a lift $\rho$ of $\mathbb{Z}_{(p)} \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ through $A$, a `CurveModel` $M_s(A)$ over the residue field of $A$ of `modularFunctionFieldFullC`, an isomorphism $e_s$ onto the corresponding fibre, and (`hsp`) a place-reduction map $r$ satisfying `IsPlaceReductionModL` and compatible with reduction of points; finally a closed point $s$ of the base with $(e_0 \ggg \mathrm{pr}_1)(x_0)$ specialising to $\varepsilon_{\inf}(s)$, and one such $A$ whose residue field $\kappa$ is algebraically closed. Under the further assumption that the set of $\kappa$-points $y$ of $M_s(A)$ with $\operatorname{ord}$ of $\bar j =$ `jqModC` $\kappa$ at the place of $y$ nonzero is infinite, the conclusion is `False`.
--
--   The statement says that on the geometric special fibre at a place above $p$ only finitely many $\kappa$-points are zeros or poles of the reduced modular invariant $\bar j$; it is recorded in the contrapositive form used by the arguments that produce infinitely many such points. It is invoked by the two results ruling out the corresponding behaviour of $j$ along the cusp section, namely [`ModularCurve.false_of_ffEquiv_symm_stalkMap_stalkSpecializes_eq_jq_mul_pow_mul_cuspSection_of_ratCurveModel_compat_of_neZero`](thm.html#ModularCurve.false_of_ffEquiv_symm_stalkMap_stalkSpecializes_eq_jq_mul_pow_mul_cuspSection_of_ratCurveModel_compat_of_neZero) and [`ModularCurve.false_of_pow_mul_ffEquiv_symm_stalkMap_stalkSpecializes_eq_jq_mul_cuspSection_of_ratCurveModel_compat_of_neZero`](thm.html#ModularCurve.false_of_pow_mul_ffEquiv_symm_stalkMap_stalkSpecializes_eq_jq_mul_cuspSection_of_ratCurveModel_compat_of_neZero).
